 "text": "Hey there! How's your day? It means the bike isn't fitting you properly. Does your saddle feel too low? Are your hands hurting after a few miles? Okay, but keep your map handy just in case. It saves you from walking long stretches, plus you' have a chat with someone. Keep your eyes on the road and stay alert. That could be the saddle slipping forward under you, or you're riding with a high stem, which lifts your head and puts your neck in an awkward angle. A good bike shop can do it for free, or you can do it yourself with a few tools. Book half an hour, and you can ask questions along the way. Most shops let you try couple of bikes in the showroom too.",
